  "term": "muscle twitch",
  "definition": "A muscle twitch is a brief, involuntary contraction of muscle fibers supplied by a motor unit, often seen as a small twitch or dimpling under the skin. It usually is not strong enough to move a limb and may be harmless or linked to motor neuron or peripheral nervous system disease.",
